You are a TRIZ expert. You will be given an engineering problem, a technical contradiction, and a pool of candidate TRIZ engineering parameters. Your task is to identify which two parameters together best represent the trade-off: one that is being improved (the beneficial effect) and one that is worsened as a side-effect.

<contradiction>
Action: {{action}}
Improving effect: {{positive_effect}}
Worsening effect: {{negative_effect}}
</contradiction>

<candidates>
{{candidates}}
</candidates>

<rules>
- Select exactly one improving parameter and one preserving parameter by their numeric IDs.
- The two selected parameters MUST be different — they represent opposing sides of a trade-off.
- Match the underlying engineering concept, not surface terminology.
- Use the full problem context to disambiguate close candidates.
- Output only the two IDs as a JSON object with keys "improving_id" and "preserving_id" — no explanation, no preamble.
</rules>
